<Study title="Huawei LLM Agent Router" kind="Projects" status="Competition project / Prompting baselines" repo="Huawei-LLM-Agent-Router" deck="Exploring how a local language model selects a tool from a Chinese-language request."><div class="study-grid"><aside><p>Tools</p><span>Python<br/>Qwen3<br/>PyTorch / Transformers</span></aside><div class="prose"><h2>One decision, two approaches.</h2><p>The runnable baseline compares a direct tool prompt with a hierarchical category-then-tool prompt. Both produce a proposed function-call string. Neither executes device actions.</p><p>The repository includes tool metadata, synthetic examples, evaluation scripts and offline routing/parser checks. The runnable implementation is <code>core/demo_agent.py</code>; <code>core/agent.py</code> remains an unfinished competition template.</p><h2>Correct name, incorrect call.</h2><p>One historical 50-case run records 17 exact-string matches and 47 function-name matches. That gap matters: choosing the right function does not establish correct arguments or safe execution. These are historical run counts, not a general benchmark.</p><div class="limitation"><h3>Current boundary</h3><p>The baseline parses text between tool tags with a regular expression. It does not validate calls against a schema or check argument types. Historical metrics predate a conversation-context evaluation fix and are not a validated multi-turn benchmark.</p></div><details><summary>Run and inspect</summary><div><p>Offline unittest checks do not need model weights. Running a baseline requires a local Qwen3-compatible model and packages appropriate for the hardware. Model weights are not included. The historical environment export is not a portable installation specification.</p><a href="https://github.com/KoreyoshiE/Huawei-LLM-Agent-Router/blob/main/core/demo_agent.py">Inspect the runnable baseline ↗</a></div></details><a class="next-study" href="/projects/omnistream/"><small>Next project</small><span>OmniStream Database Project ↗</span></a></div></div></Study>
